Template: abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/abraflexi-url
Type: string
Default:
Description: AbraFlexi server URL used to read changed documents:
 Address of the AbraFlexi server whose webhooks are accepted, e.g.
 https://abraflexi.example.com:5434. The acceptor reads the changed invoices
 from it to derive meta-states (settled, reminders, ...). Leave empty to
 configure it by hand in /etc/abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/.env.

Template: abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/abraflexi-company
Type: string
Default:
Description: AbraFlexi company (default):
 Company code in AbraFlexi used when the webhook does not name one.

Template: abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/abraflexi-login
Type: string
Default:
Description: AbraFlexi login:
 User the acceptor reads documents as (read-only access is enough).

Template: abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/abraflexi-password
Type: password
Default:
Description: AbraFlexi password:
 Password of the AbraFlexi user above. It is stored in the debconf database
 (readable by root only) and written to /etc/abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/.env,
 so it survives package upgrades.

Template: abraflexi-webhook-acceptor/allowed-companies
Type: string
Default:
Description: Companies the acceptor may read from (comma separated):
 Webhooks naming any other company are not looked up in AbraFlexi.
 Leave empty for a single-company installation.
